# A widget function's blueprint as a supplier's answer, its result an event: a computed
# answer, a tick late (Semantics ch. 9, "How a supplier answers": "A computed answer is the
# next tick's input. An event output's firing at n [..] is delivered to the child's place
# as an input of tick n+1, and tick n+1 is owed"; its negative space, "No prompt computed
# answer"). `@Relayed !tap` builds a place of its own under the supplier's row and gives
# the host's own event back: the child counts the host's click in the next tick, as it
# does under `@ !tap` (sem-ch09-host-delay). Written by Claude on the claude-lowering
# branch; subject to change.
emit Ui.*
test mod Tests
use Ui.*

@child: @unit
@child:
    !hit <- Ui.Button($label=$"hit")                              # 0, answered by the host's !tap
    $hits <- 0 then $hits + 1 on !hit
    Ui.Label($text=$"{$hits} hits")                               # 1, forwarded

@Relayed: fn !a -> @!a
fn @Relayed !taps:
    Ui.Label($text=$"relaying")                                   # 0
    @ !taps

@host: @unit
@host:
    !tap <- Ui.Button($label=$"tap")                              # 0
    ignore <- @HostDocument @child, \|p, e| match e:              # 1/[p]
        Ui.Button(..): @Relayed !tap
        otherwise: @Element e
    $taps <- 0 then $taps + 1 on !tap
    Ui.Label($text=$"{$taps} taps")                               # 2
